#!/usr/bin/env bash
# ZorpOS recovery guide. Plain English, no glyphs. Weird must never mean bricked.
cat <<'TXT'
ZORPOS RECOVERY (Earthling edition)
===================================

1. Get a text console on an installed system
   - At the boot menu pick "ZorpOS (LTS kernel, safe graphics)" - linux-lts, nomodeset.
   - Or press "e" on any entry and append:   systemd.unit=multi-user.target
     That skips the graphical greeter entirely and gives you TTY logins.
   - Already in the desktop and it's stuck?   Ctrl+Alt+F3   (any of F2-F6).

2. Turn the alien shell off (from a TTY)
   - zorp-escape-hatch            explains every escape route
   - Earthling Mode for your user: touch ~/.config/zorpos/earthling
   - Disable the graphical login:  sudo systemctl disable greetd && sudo reboot

3. Repair a system that will not boot (from this live ISO)
   lsblk -f                                   # find your root (and EFI) partition
   mount /dev/<root> /mnt                     # e.g. /dev/nvme0n1p2
   mount /dev/<efi>  /mnt/boot                # if you have a separate ESP
   arch-chroot /mnt
     pacman -Syu                              # finish an interrupted upgrade
     mkinitcpio -P                            # rebuild initramfs for all kernels
     bootctl install   # or: grub-install && grub-mkconfig -o /boot/grub/grub.cfg
   exit; umount -R /mnt; reboot

4. Everything underneath is Arch Linux. The Arch Wiki applies:
   https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/General_troubleshooting
TXT
